Assertions:
[ASSERT] INDEXED contains {{pageA}} exactly once with Status Published {SPEC}
[ASSERT] the indexed title equals {{pageATitle}} (the value in Sanity), not {{pageADecoy}} that the signed body carried: the payload is a notification {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] the xAPI pageDocument id equals the REST id {{pageA}} and its Content hero.asset.url is non-empty (cross-layer equality REST == xAPI) {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] after the signed delete {{pageA}} is absent from INDEXED and slugInfo no longer resolves {{pageAPermalink}} to it {SPEC}

[ASSERT] the set of _type values across INDEXED has exactly one member, virtoPage (the legacy PageType) {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] {{settingsDoc}} and {{footer}} (types not configured) are absent from INDEXED {SPEC}
[ASSERT] {{pageA}} is present in INDEXED {OBSERVED}

[ASSERT] PHASE 1: {{pageA}}, {{footer}} and {{settingsDoc}} are all in INDEXED (the three types parsed from ' virtoPage , footerNavigation;siteSettings') {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] PHASE 1: {{landing}} (type not in the list) is NOT in INDEXED {SPEC}
[ASSERT] PHASE 2: INDEXED contains {{settingsDoc}} and no virtoPage document, although the hidden legacy PageType is virtoPage (it was indexed in the legacy case and in PHASE 1): DocumentTypes wins over PageType {SPEC}{OBSERVED}

[ASSERT] TA equals {{titleP}} and is not {{titleS}} {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] TB equals {{titleS}} and is not {{titleP}}: moving isPriority flips the winner {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] TC equals {{titleS}}: without isPriority the first configured dataset wins {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] {{conflict}} appears exactly once in INDEXED in every phase {SPEC}

[ASSERT] IDX_PER_DATASET contains {{landing}} (landing is listed for the secondary dataset) {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] IDX_PER_DATASET does NOT contain {{landingInProd}}: landing is not listed for the primary dataset {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] IDX_INHERIT contains {{secPage}} and does NOT contain {{landing}}: the dataset without documentTypes inherits Sanity.DocumentTypes (virtoPage only) {SPEC}{OBSERVED}

[ASSERT] IDX_A contains {{secPage}} (the valid entry is indexed) and the rebuild did not fail {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] IDX_A contains no document that exists only in the primary dataset: the entry without projectId contributed nothing {SPEC}
[ASSERT] IDX_B contains {{pageA}}: invalid JSON falls back to the single-project settings {SPEC}{OBSERVED}

[ASSERT] IDX_A contains {{pageA}} (the entry with ${qaToken} resolved) {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] IDX_A contains no document that exists only in the secondary dataset ({{secPage}}): the ${notDefined} entry was skipped, the other entry was still indexed {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] IDX_B1 contains {{pageA}} (Sanity.ApiToken reference resolved) {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] IDX_B2 contains no Sanity document: Sanity.ApiToken = ${notDefined} skips the project instead of sending the literal {SPEC}{OBSERVED}

[ASSERT] NAMES does not contain Sanity.Projects and does not contain Sanity.ApiToken {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] the only name in NAMES is Sanity.Enabled {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] ADMIN_SET contains Sanity.Projects and Sanity.ApiToken in at least one of the up-to-5 store/search responses (the admin API has them, so the absence above is meaningful) {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] PUB_PROJECTS is false and PUB_TOKEN is false (the setting descriptors are not public) {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] RESP contains neither the project id of Sanity.Projects nor any token value {SPEC}

[ASSERT] S_NOSIG is HTTP 401 {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] S_BADSECRET is HTTP 401 {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] S_LEGACY is HTTP 401 (documented breaking change) {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] AFTER equals BEFORE: a rejected delivery changed nothing in the index {SPEC}

[ASSERT] S0 is HTTP 200 and S1 is HTTP 200: both configured secrets are accepted {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] T_MINUS4 is HTTP 200: inside the 300 s tolerance {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] T_MINUS10 is HTTP 401 and T_PLUS10 is HTTP 401: 600 s is outside the 300 s tolerance in both directions {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] T_SECONDS is HTTP 401 {OBSERVED}

[ASSERT] S_TAMPER is HTTP 401 {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] S_BIG (signed, 10.5 MB body) is HTTP 401 {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] S_CONTROL (same delivery, no padding) is HTTP 200, so the 401 above comes from the size and not from the signature {OBSERVED}

[ASSERT] S_ID, S_OP and S_DS are each HTTP 400 {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] S_BADID_BODY and S_BADID_HEADER are each HTTP 400 {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] {{pageA}} and {{pageB}} are still in INDEXED: no contradicting delivery deleted or replaced anything {SPEC}

[ASSERT] S_UNLISTED, S_TYPE and S_PROJECT are each HTTP 200 (a rejected-by-scope delivery is not an error for Sanity, which would retry) {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] AFTER contains neither {{unlisted}} nor {{landingInProd}} {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] AFTER has no document whose source project is AGENT-TEST-unknown and the document set equals BEFORE apart from pages already indexed {OBSERVED}

[ASSERT] the reference to {{pageA}} has slug equal to {{pageAPermalink}} (permalink.current) {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] the reference to {{pageB}} has slug equal to {{pageBSeoSlug}} (only seo.slug exists) {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] the nested reference at depth 3 has a slug equal to its target's link {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] the reference to {{settingsDoc}} (no slug) and the reference to a missing document have NO slug property {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] the image asset reference {{imageId}} has url equal to {{imageUrl}} and the file asset reference {{fileId}} has url equal to {{fileUrl}} (the URLs Sanity returned on upload) {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] the malformed asset reference is unchanged: no url property was added {SPEC}{OBSERVED}

[ASSERT] LOG has a line naming each reason: missing signature header, no matching secret, timestamp outside the window, header different from the signed value, invalid document id {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] LOG has a not-found warning naming the document, the project and the dataset {OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] LOG has warnings for an unresolved ${name}, a source conflict (winner and loser source) and invalid Sanity.Projects JSON {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
[ASSERT] none of the SECRETS values occurs in LOG (0 occurrences each) {SPEC}{OBSERVED}
